   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• OLED on 3V3, not 5V, otherwise module may pull SDA/SCL up to VCC.\n• LD2450 needs 5V power, but its UART is 3.3 V logic, so TX/RX wire straight to the XIAO.\n• Buttons: D0 and D1 to GND, internal pull-ups. Lines that cross without a dot aren't connected.\n• Grey pins are unused. UART 256000 baud, I2C SDA GPIO8 / SCL GPIO9.",
   "originalText": "• OLED on 3V3, not 5V, otherwise module may pull SDA/SCL up to VCC.\n• LD2450 needs 5V power, but its UART is 3.3 V logic, so TX/RX wire straight to the XIAO.\n• Buttons: D0 and D1 to GND, internal pull-ups. Lines that cross without a dot aren't connected.\n• Grey pins are unused. UART 256000 baud, I2C SDA GPIO8 / SCL GPIO9.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
